-- title:
--   Triviality of inertia in radical extensions away from n
-- statement:
--   Let $E$ and $M$ be number fields with $M$ an $E$-algebra, let $n$ be a natural number, let $u \in E$ and $\alpha \in M$ satisfy $\alpha^{n} = u$ (the image of $u$ under the structure map $E \to M$), and assume that the identity is the only $E$-algebra automorphism of $M$ fixing $\alpha$, i.e. $\sigma\alpha = \alpha$ forces $\sigma = 1$ for $\sigma \in M \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[E]} M$ (this holds, for instance, when $M = E(\alpha)$). Let $v$ be a height-one prime of the ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_E$, and assume that the $v$-adic valuation of $u$, computed on $E$, equals $1$, and that the image of $n$ in $\mathcal{O}_E$ does not lie in the prime ideal of $v$. Finally let $w$ be an element of `v.Extension (NumberField.RingOfIntegers M)`, that is, a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_M$ whose contraction to $\mathcal{O}_E$ is $v$. The conclusion is that the inertia subgroup of the prime ideal of $w$ relative to the group $M \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[E]} M$ of $E$-algebra automorphisms of $M$ is the trivial subgroup.
--
--   This is the statement that a radical (Kummer) extension generated by an $n$-th root of a $v$-unit is unramified at $v$ when $v$ does not divide $n$, formulated for the inertia subgroup of the full automorphism group $\mathrm{Aut}_E(M)$ rather than for a Galois group, so that nothing is assumed about $M/E$ being Galois. It is used on the norm side of the second inequality of class field theory, in [`NumberField.PrimeNormIndex.secondInequalityCTM_of_primitiveRoots`](thm.html#NumberField.PrimeNormIndex.secondInequalityCTM_of_primitiveRoots) and in the construction of auxiliary Galois extensions with prescribed local behaviour.
